@@ -0,0 +1,32 @@
+# Experimental Lumion LiveSync
+
+File > Start Lumion LiveSync publishes the model's tessellated solids and RGB surface colors to a separate local adapter.
+Open Lumion first. Stop through File > Stop Lumion LiveSync before closing Lumion. No network listener or automatic startup is added.
+Model snapshots follow edits, undo, redo and project replacement; pending snapshots are coalesced. Export is limited to 150,000 triangles
+and 64 MiB per JSON frame. Coordinates convert from BIMCraft millimetres/Z up to metres/Y up. Root model meshes are keyed by persistent
+element GUID and surface color; linked display geometry currently uses its synthetic display owner id. Material names are keyed by color.
+Color changes replace that color group, so Lumion material overrides are not guaranteed to survive recoloring.
+
+This adapter does not transfer image/procedural textures, UVs, transparency, BIM properties, cameras, lights, annotations or point clouds.
+It publishes the full tessellated model, not a selected view's visibility settings. The first version rebuilds mesh data on edits.
+Status says published rather than claiming reception. Lumion remains the receiver; it is never launched or terminated by BIMCraft.
+
+## Private local engine files
+
+The public repository contains only original adapter source, not Act-3D binaries. Compile Bridge.cs with the 64-bit .NET Framework C# compiler,
+referencing System.Core.dll, System.Numerics.dll and System.Web.Extensions.dll. Tests.cs can be compiled with Bridge.cs using /main:BridgeTests.
+Place the resulting BIMCraft-Lumion-Bridge.exe in a lumion subfolder next to bimcraft.exe, together with LiveSyncEngineNET.dll and
+LiveSyncCoreNET.dll from the user's LiveSync 26.1.8 installer. The adapter checks pinned SHA-256 hashes before loading either DLL.
+It refuses other versions. Do not redistribute vendor DLLs without establishing the applicable rights.
+
+The adapter has no general file or command endpoint: it accepts only length-prefixed geometry snapshots on standard input.
+It validates frame lengths, schema version, counts, key lengths, duplicate keys, material references and finite numeric ranges.
+It removes stale geometry, keeps writer identities on edits, and deletes its own LiveSync document at EOF. A stalled adapter is terminated
+after a two-second shutdown grace period. Native engine crashes are isolated from BIMCraft.
+
+## Verification status
+
+A user-run connection test on Lumion 2026.1.5 displayed a white box on 23 October 2026. Geometry reception is confirmed by that observation.
+The original probe did not separately publish its material. The adapter now publishes material elements, but material color, continuous model
+updates, deletion, scene replacement and large-model performance still require end-to-end verification in Lumion.
+Local compilation does not establish runtime compatibility or complete security certification.
